{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/26975-bronze-age-solar-real-life-edition","id":26975,"title":"Bronze Age Solar? - Real Life Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-09T21:06:16-08:00","id":26975,"title":"Bronze Age Solar? - Real Life Edition","content":"From the Life imitating Art Ahead of Its Time Department...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Archaeologists in the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shahr-e_Sukhteh\" target=\"_blank\">Burnt City</a> have discovered what appears to be an ancient prosthetic eye. What makes this discovery exceptionally awesome is the striking description of how the owner and her false eye would have appeared while she was still alive and blinking:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> [The eye] has a hemispherical form and a diameter of just over 2.5 cm (1 inch). It consists of very light material, probably bitumen paste. <b>The surface of the artificial eye is covered with a thin layer of gold, engraved with a central circle (representing the iris) and gold lines patterned like sun rays</b>. The female remains found with the artificial eye was 1.82 m tall (6 feet), much taller than ordinary women of her time. On both sides of the eye are drilled tiny holes, through which a golden thread could hold the eyeball in place. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burnt_city\" target=\"_blank\">Since microscopic research has shown that the eye socket showed clear imprints of the golden thread, the eyeball must have been worn during her lifetime</a>. The woman\u2019s skeleton has been dated to between 2900 and 2800 BCE. <br /> </div>So she was an extraordinarily tall woman walking around wearing an engraved golden eye patterned with rays like a tiny sun. What an awesome sight that must have been. </div> </div> </div>So they didn't stop at just having a prosthetic eye around 2800 BCE. No, it's a golden eye with rays of a sun design upon it. I think the artwork offered up within said thread made it immediately &quot;Solar&quot; to me, but that's just where my mind has been lately.<br /> <br /> Even without the idea of &quot;hey this is practically something out of Exalted!&quot; aspect, I found this to be really cool. Have there been any other archeological finds people have noted to be rather Creation-like? <br /> <br /> <br /> Source: <a href=\"http://ursulavernon.tumblr.com/post/69544392704/kitsunecoffee-beecharts-fangirequeen\" target=\"_blank\">http://ursulavernon.tumblr.com/post/...s-fangirequeen</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1225-naz","name":"Naz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1225_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T21:44:01-08:00","id":26983,"title":"","content":"The underground tomb/necropolis of the first Qin Emperor is my usual gold standard, esp if it turns out to live up to the legends surrounding it! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mausoleum_of_the_First_Qin_Emperor\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Tomb_of_the_First_Emperor_Qin_Shi_Huang_Di%2C_Xi%27an%2C_China_-_panoramio.jpg/1280px-Tomb_of_the_First_Emperor_Qin_Shi_Huang_Di%2C_Xi%27an%2C_China_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mausoleum_of_the_First_Qin_Emperor\" target=\"_blank\"> Mausoleum of Qin Shi Huang - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mausoleum_of_the_First_Qin_Emperor\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mausoleum_of_the_First_Qin_Emperor </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As for the eye, I love the implied awesomeness of the woman...like, &quot;If I gotta have a fake eye, then it may as well look badass!&quot; Also, I love the title of &quot;the Burnt City&quot;, tho I can imagine the inhabitants to be pretty dismayed if time travellers called it that in front of them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T07:23:00-08:00","id":27167,"title":"","content":"Sidenote: A place called the Burnt City?<br /> <br /> Dude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fabian, Twelfth Night</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this were play'd upon a stage now, I could condemn it as an improbable fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T07:54:45-08:00","id":27191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/26975-bronze-age-solar-real-life-edition?p=27167#post27167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidenote: A place called the Burnt City?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Other kings said it was daft to build a castle in the Fire Swamp, but I built it all the same, just to show 'em. It burnt down in the swamp. So! I built a second one. That burnt down in the swamp. So I built a third one! That sank, fell over, then burnt down in the swamp. But the <i>fourth</i> one stayed up! And that's what you're gonna get lad; the strongest castle on this peninsula.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T10:29:00-08:00","id":27294,"title":"","content":"On a more serious note, this is the kind of thing I'm talking about when I suggest that Crafts is primarily about using creativity and materials at hand to come up with solutions. Making an effective prosthetic out of asphalt and gold leaf? Think of the mindset that comes up with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T11:13:39-08:00","id":27326,"title":"","content":"strongly considering finding a way to working the Golden-Eyed Queen of the Burnt City into the setting now somehow","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T12:29:55-08:00","id":27390,"title":"","content":"That truly is an amazing inspiration for Exalted. By the way, taller than the ordinary women<i> of her time</i>? I think even today one would be hard pressed to find many places where the average woman is that tall...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T12:39:20-08:00","id":27404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/26975-bronze-age-solar-real-life-edition?p=27390#post27390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That truly is an amazing inspiration for Exalted. By the way, taller than the ordinary women<i> of her time</i>? I think even today one would be hard pressed to find many places where the average woman is that tall...</div> </div> </div> </div>And there have been times and places where the average woman would be even taller.<br /> <br /> Not all reference points for contemporary comparisons emerge from an assumption that things have consistently followed a growth curve that amounts to &quot;past = less&quot;.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:09:37-08:00","id":27648,"title":"","content":"I didn't think anyone would miss the Burnt City aspect. Even the proper name - Shahr-e Sukhteh - could find a place in Creation, I'm sure. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/26975-bronze-age-solar-real-life-edition?p=27326#post27326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">strongly considering finding a way to working the Golden-Eyed Queen of the Burnt City into the setting now somehow</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1225-naz","name":"Naz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1225_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:59:41-08:00","id":27680,"title":"","content":"Don't you all see?<br /> A destroyed city!<br /> A woman of improbably stature!<br /> <br /> This isn't any eye. This is THE eye.<br /> They've found the eye of autocthon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1397-parallel","name":"Parallel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T20:38:41-08:00","id":27725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/26975-bronze-age-solar-real-life-edition?p=27404#post27404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And there have been times and places where the average woman would be even taller.<br /> <br /> Not all reference points for contemporary comparisons emerge from an assumption that things have consistently followed a growth curve that amounts to &quot;past = less&quot;.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Re-reading my own post it is clear I did not express myself properly. I meant &quot;even today&quot; to imply &quot;in all the time between then and now&quot; (though now that I think of it I should also have included the time before that as well, since what I actually had in mind is &quot;I don't think humanity ever had average, ordinary women that tall&quot;). I was not aware there have ever been some place and time in which women <i>averaged </i>taller than 1,82m. Have you got any examples?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T12:57:12-08:00","id":29476,"title":"","content":"Really, <i>anyone</i> got an example? I have been searching the web and any printed encyclopedias I have here and can't find anywhere info on any period on which an average woman would be taller than that. I'm super curious now XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T12:06:31-08:00","id":30031,"title":"","content":"All the information I've found for modern day puts average female height at about 5'2&quot; and the average in various countries around the world goes from 4'8&quot; to 5'7&quot;. <a href=\"http://www.wolframalpha.com/input/?i=Average+female+height&amp;a=*C.female-_*CommonAttributeValue-\" target=\"_blank\">One source</a>.<br /> <br /> Have not found a solid study really delving into historical height prior to the last few hundred years. Did not find anything to suggest a woman's average height was ever 6 foot / 1.82 cm, but understood that lack of data is not necessarily proof.<br /> <br /> <br /> I took note of the following paragraph on <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_height\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia</a> for context on how wildly height may vary within a specific region in a mere handful of generations:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the late nineteenth century, the Netherlands was a land renowned for its short population, but today its population is among the world's tallest with young men averaging 1.84 m (6 ft 0 in) tall<i><sup>.</sup></i> The tallest average in Europe is in the Dinaric Alps, with young men averaging 1.86 m (6 ft 1 in), and young women averaging 1.71 m (5 ft 7 in). </div> </div> </div>This also led me to find the following article looking at how the Dutch may have become so tall inside of 150 years: <a href=\"http://suite101.com/a/why-are-the-dutch-so-tall-a55753\" target=\"_blank\">http://suite101.com/a/why-are-the-dutch-so-tall-a55753</a><br /> <br /> This particular article makes mention to the following:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Northern Europe, human height reached a maximum around 800 A.D., but then dropped to a minimum in the 17th century before climbing back up again. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps 800 AD can give a lead for further investigation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1225,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1225-naz","user":"Naz","date":". 12-14-2013, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1225-naz","name":"Naz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1225_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}